From: canoziia <canoziia@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] scheduler: balance established decodes across PP batches

Model Runner V2 + pipeline parallelism + async scheduling lets a decode request
advance only once every `pp_size` scheduler steps, because the worker-side
sampled-token broadcast ring consumes a step-T result at T+pp_size (#42187).
The scheduler has no corresponding fairness term, so one step can take most of
the established decodes while the other in-flight batches stay short.
vllm#50853 lists this as an open gap ("a burst can fill the global request
slots in one batch and leave later PP batches empty").

Measured on our six-GPU SM80 DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash box (PP=6, DSpark K=5,
max_num_seqs=32) with the worker step tracer at sample_every=1, concurrency 32,
feature off: 79% of steps carried <=2 requests while 203 steps carried 26
(median 2, max 26). Requests admitted together lock into one cohort and then
advance and stall together.

Add an opt-in share limit: a step takes at most
ceil(max_num_seqs / pp_size) established decode requests, where "established"
is evaluated before the request is scheduled
(`num_computed_tokens >= num_prompt_tokens`). Prefill requests, prefill chunks
and the chunk that completes a prompt are never capped, so the token budget
stays free to absorb new work. A deferred request simply remains eligible, so
no state changes and no starvation is introduced; the count is restored if a
selected request is preempted later in the same step. The cadence, the ring and
the collective order are untouched.

Off by default; set VLLM_PP_DECODE_COHORT_BALANCE=1 to enable. One image
therefore serves both sides of an A/B.

A/B on that box, same image, only the env var differing, 3 runs each, tracer
off, same prompts and output budget:

  conc  tokens/s off   tokens/s on    delta
  16         356          347        -2.3%  (spread 270-361 -> 340-351)
  32         255          614      +141.1%  (spread 254-288 -> 603-615)

and with the tracer on at concurrency 32 the composition becomes what the cap
intends: median requests/step 2 -> 6 (== ceil(32/6)), max 26 -> 20, steps with
<=2 requests 79% -> 21%.

This follows the decode-only form discussed on vllm#50410, not that PR's global
request cap: per that thread the global cap measured -8.21% throughput and
+11.31% mean TTFT against doing nothing, while the decode-only form measured
+22.95%.

Signed-off-by: canoziia <canoziia@users.noreply.github.com>
---
--- a/vllm/envs.py
+++ b/vllm/envs.py
@@ -48,6 +48,7 @@
     VLLM_TRACE_FUNCTION: int = 0
     VLLM_USE_FLASHINFER_SAMPLER: bool = True
     VLLM_PP_LAYER_PARTITION: str | None = None
+    VLLM_PP_DECODE_COHORT_BALANCE: bool = False
     VLLM_CPU_OFFLOAD_GB_PER_RANK: str | None = None
     VLLM_ENGRAM_EXACT_PIN: bool = True
     VLLM_CPU_KVCACHE_SPACE: int | None = 0
@@ -905,6 +906,12 @@
     ),
     # Pipeline stage partition strategy
     "VLLM_PP_LAYER_PARTITION": lambda: os.getenv("VLLM_PP_LAYER_PARTITION", None),
+    # Cap established decode requests per scheduler step so MRV2 + PP + async
+    # spreads them across the `pp_size` in-flight pipeline batches. Does not
+    # change the PP decode cadence itself.
+    "VLLM_PP_DECODE_COHORT_BALANCE": lambda: bool(
+        int(os.getenv("VLLM_PP_DECODE_COHORT_BALANCE", "0"))
+    ),
     # Per-PP-rank UVA offload budget (GiB, comma-separated, indexed by PP
     # rank). Overrides --cpu-offload-gb for the matching rank so heavily
     # loaded pipeline stages can offload more than lighter ones.
--- a/vllm/v1/core/sched/scheduler.py
+++ b/vllm/v1/core/sched/scheduler.py
@@ -7,6 +7,7 @@
 from dataclasses import replace
 from typing import Any
 
+from vllm import envs
 from vllm.compilation.cuda_graph import CUDAGraphStat
 from vllm.config import KVEventsConfig, VllmConfig
 from vllm.distributed.ec_transfer.ec_connector.base import (
@@ -323,6 +324,32 @@
 
         self.use_pp = self.parallel_config.pipeline_parallel_size > 1
         self.use_v2_model_runner = vllm_config.use_v2_model_runner
+        # MRV2 + PP + async lets a decode request advance only once every
+        # `pp_size` steps: the sampled-token broadcast ring consumes a step-T
+        # result at T+pp_size. Nothing spreads the requests over those
+        # in-flight batches, so one step can take most of the established
+        # decodes and leave the other steps short. Cap each step with a share
+        # of them; prefill work is never capped.
+        self.pp_decode_cohort_target = 0
+        self._pp_scheduled_decode_ids: set[str] = set()
+        if (
+            envs.VLLM_PP_DECODE_COHORT_BALANCE
+            and self.use_v2_model_runner
+            and self.use_pp
+            and vllm_config.scheduler_config.async_scheduling
+        ):
+            pp_size = self.parallel_config.pipeline_parallel_size
+            # ceil(max_num_seqs / pp_size)
+            self.pp_decode_cohort_target = max(
+                1, -(-self.max_num_running_reqs // pp_size)
+            )
+            logger.info(
+                "PP decode-cohort balancing: <=%d established decodes per "
+                "step (max_num_seqs=%d, pp_size=%d)",
+                self.pp_decode_cohort_target,
+                self.max_num_running_reqs,
+                pp_size,
+            )
         # Scheduler iteration counter. Drives the V2+PP+async decode-throttle
         # cadence (`next_decode_eligible_step`).
         self.current_step = 0
@@ -563,6 +590,7 @@
 
     def schedule(self, throttle_prefills: bool = False) -> SchedulerOutput:
         self.current_step += 1
+        self._pp_scheduled_decode_ids.clear()
         # NOTE(woosuk) on the scheduling algorithm:
         # There's no "decoding phase" nor "prefill phase" in the scheduler.
         # Each request just has the num_computed_tokens and
@@ -639,6 +667,19 @@
                 req_index += 1
                 continue
 
+            is_established_decode = (
+                self.pp_decode_cohort_target > 0
+                and request.num_computed_tokens >= request.num_prompt_tokens
+            )
+            if (
+                is_established_decode
+                and len(self._pp_scheduled_decode_ids)
+                >= self.pp_decode_cohort_target
+            ):
+                # Defer it to a step that has room; it stays eligible meanwhile.
+                req_index += 1
+                continue
+
             if defer_prefills and request.is_prefill_chunk:
                 # DP prefill balancing: defer this in-progress prefill chunk to a
                 # cadence-aligned step; decodes still run to fill this step.
@@ -770,6 +811,7 @@
                         if preempted_req in scheduled_running_reqs:
                             preempted_req_id = preempted_req.request_id
                             scheduled_running_reqs.remove(preempted_req)
+                            self._pp_scheduled_decode_ids.discard(preempted_req_id)
                             restored = num_scheduled_tokens.pop(preempted_req_id)
                             token_budget += restored
                             input_budget += restored + draft_slots
@@ -807,6 +849,8 @@
             scheduled_running_reqs.append(request)
             prefill_scheduled |= request.is_prefill_chunk
             request_id = request.request_id
+            if is_established_decode:
+                self._pp_scheduled_decode_ids.add(request_id)
             req_to_new_blocks[request_id] = new_blocks
             num_scheduled_tokens[request_id] = num_new_tokens
             token_budget -= num_new_tokens
